# Largest Independent Set in Binary Trees

## Problem Description
Given a binary tree, find the size of the Largest Independent Set (LIS). A subset of nodes is an independent set if there is no edge between any two nodes in the subset. The size of the LIS is the maximum number of nodes in such a subset.

You need to implement three different approaches to solve this problem:
1. A naive recursive solution
2. A memoized dynamic programming solution
3. An iterative dynamic programming solution using post-order traversal

## Class and Function Requirements
You must implement the following exactly as specified:

```cpp
struct Node {
    int data;
    Node* left;
