# String Analysis Problem

## Problem Description
Write a C++ function that performs comprehensive analysis and comparison between two input strings. The function should return a map containing various comparison results and statistical information about the strings.

## Function Requirements
Implement the following function exactly as specified:

```cpp
map<string, string> analyze_strings(const string& str1, const string& str2)
```

The function should return a map with the following key-value pairs:
- "string1": The first input string
- "string2": The second input string
- "length1": Length of the first string (as string)
- "length2": Length of the second string (as string)
- "lexical_compare": Result of lexical comparison ("equal", "greater", or "less")
- "last_char_diff": Difference between last characters' ASCII values (as string), or 0 if either string is empty
- "case_sensitive_equal": "true" if strings are equal ignoring case, "false" otherwise
- "digits_in_str1": Count of digit characters in first string (as string)
- "digits_in_str2": Count of digit characters in second string (as string)
- "special_in_str1": Count of special (non-alphanumeric) characters in first string (as string)
- "special_in_str2": Count of special (non-alphanumeric) characters in second string (as string)

## Example Usage
```cpp
auto result = analyze_strings("Hello", "world");
// result will contain:
// {
//     {"string1", "Hello"},
//     {"string2", "world"},
//     {"length1", "5"},
//     {"length2", "5"},
//     {"lexical_compare", "less"},
//     {"last_char_diff", "11"},
//     {"case_sensitive_equal", "false"},
//     {"digits_in_str1", "0"},
//     {"digits_in_str2", "0"},
//     {"special_in_str1", "0"},
//     {"special_in_str2", "0"}
// }
```

## Constraints
- The input strings can be of any length (including empty)
- The function should handle all ASCII characters
- All numeric results should be returned as strings
- Case sensitivity should be considered only for the "case_sensitive_equal" field
- Special characters are defined as any non-alphanumeric characters

## Evaluation Criteria
- Correct implementation of all specified comparisons and analyses
- Proper handling of edge cases (empty strings, special characters, etc.)
- Accurate conversion of numeric values to strings
- Efficient string processing

## Note
Do not modify the function signature. Your solution must exactly match the specified interface.

