# Terrain Model Generation

## Problem Description
You are tasked with implementing a terrain model generator that converts a height grid into a 3D mesh suitable for rendering. The system should generate vertices, normals, texture coordinates, and triangle indices for the terrain mesh based on a given height grid.

## Class Requirements
You must implement the following structures exactly as specified:

### Vec3 Structure
```cpp
struct Vec3 {
    float x, y, z;

    Vec3(float x = 0, float y = 0, float z = 0) : x(x), y(y), z(z) {}

    bool operator==(const Vec3& other) const {
        return x == other.x && y == other.y && z == other.z;
    }
};
```

### HeightGrid Structure
```cpp
struct HeightGrid {
    int sizeX, sizeZ;
    vector<vector<Vec3>> data;

    HeightGrid(int x, int z) : sizeX(x), sizeZ(z), data(x, vector<Vec3>(z)) {}

    Vec3& at(int x, int z) { 
        if (x < 0 || x >= sizeX || z < 0 || z >= sizeZ)
            throw out_of_range("Grid index out of range");
        return data[x][z]; 
    }

    const Vec3& at(int x, int z) const { 
        if (x < 0 || x >= sizeX || z < 0 || z >= sizeZ)
            throw out_of_range("Grid index out of range");
        return data[x][z]; 
    }
};
```

### Model Structure
```cpp
struct Model {
    vector<float> vertices;
    vector<float> normals;
    vector<float> texCoords;
    vector<unsigned int> indices;
};
```

## Required Functions
You must implement the following helper functions and the main generation function:

### Vector Math Functions
```cpp
Vec3 vectorSub(const Vec3& a, const Vec3& b);
Vec3 crossProduct(const Vec3& a, const Vec3& b);
Vec3 vectorAdd(const Vec3& a, const Vec3& b);
Vec3 scalarMult(const Vec3& v, float s);
float vectorLength(const Vec3& v);
Vec3 normalize(const Vec3& v);
```

### Vertex Access Function
```cpp
Vec3 getVertex(const vector<float>& vertexArray, int x, int z, const HeightGrid& grid);
```

### Normal Calculation Function
```cpp
Vec3 calculateNormal(const vector<float>& vertexArray, int x, int z, const HeightGrid& grid);
```

### Main Generation Function
```cpp
Model generateTerrain(const HeightGrid& heightGrid, bool generateZeroHeight = false, int resolution = 1);
```

## Problem Specifications
1. The `generateTerrain` function should:
   - Create a terrain mesh from the given height grid
   - Handle edge cases (single point grid, rectangular grids)
   - Support resolution scaling (vertex spacing)
   - Generate proper normals using the cross product of adjacent triangles
   - Generate proper texture coordinates
   - Generate proper triangle indices

2. Constraints:
   - Resolution must be positive (throw invalid_argument if not)
   - Grid indices must be within bounds (throw out_of_range if not)
   - The solution must be in C++
   - You must use the exact class/function signatures provided

## Example Usage
```cpp
int main() {
    // Create a 3x3 height grid
    HeightGrid grid(3, 3);

    // Set some height values
    grid.at(0, 0) = Vec3(0, 1, 0);
    grid.at(1, 1) = Vec3(0, 2, 0);
    grid.at(2, 2) = Vec3(0, 3, 0);

    // Generate terrain model
    Model terrain = generateTerrain(grid);

    // Generate terrain with zero height and resolution 2
    Model flatTerrain = generateTerrain(grid, true, 2);

    return 0;
}
```

## Notes
- The height grid stores Vec3 values, but only the y-component is used for height
- Texture coordinates should be generated using the grid indices
- Normals should be calculated by averaging the cross products of adjacent triangles
- The solution should handle grids of any size (1x1 up to large grids)

